WEBVTT

00:04.780 --> 00:07.230
<i>I worked as a salaryman 
for a toxic company,</i>

00:07.230 --> 00:09.070
<i>until I reincarnated...</i>

00:09.070 --> 00:12.900
<i>in a crazy world where everything is 
dropped by monsters in dungeons.</i>

00:13.420 --> 00:18.350
<i>In my new life, I'm level 1, 
but I have a unique skill</i>

00:18.350 --> 00:20.550
<i>that puts all of my drop rates at rank S.</i>

00:21.200 --> 00:23.220
<i>And today I'm facing off against...</i>

00:23.220 --> 00:24.880
<i>a rare monster?!</i>

00:24.880 --> 00:28.540
<i>I had no idea drops from monsters 
could be used that way!</i>

00:36.140 --> 00:45.230
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

02:00.010 --> 02:05.020
<b>Moving to a New Place!

Just Relaxing at Home</b>

02:05.020 --> 02:08.140
<b>Telulu Level 4</b>

02:10.690 --> 02:13.740
Th-That's a rare monster!

02:13.740 --> 02:14.620
What?!

02:15.570 --> 02:17.020
You're not getting away!

02:22.220 --> 02:23.770
What's this?

02:23.770 --> 02:27.370
That's the first time I've seen 
a rare monster drop anything!

02:27.980 --> 02:29.090
Emily...

02:31.070 --> 02:32.240
Emily,

02:32.480 --> 02:35.090
would you put this on?

02:35.370 --> 02:38.010
What? Y-You mean...

02:38.430 --> 02:41.340
I want you to have it.

02:42.480 --> 02:45.930
You've made me so happy! 
I'll treasure this!

02:45.930 --> 02:47.440
Great!

02:47.440 --> 02:50.240
Now you can rake in the profits for us!

02:50.440 --> 02:53.540
Huh? Rake in... profits?

02:53.540 --> 02:57.580
Oh, I guess you can't hear it, 
like with the seeds and stuff.

02:57.570 --> 03:04.160
<b>Put on</b>

02:57.570 --> 03:04.160
<b>Fight as usual</b>

02:57.570 --> 03:04.160
<b>Double drops</b>

02:58.160 --> 03:00.600
I heard a voice when I picked that up.

03:00.600 --> 03:04.150
It's apparently a necklace 
that doubles item drops!

03:04.450 --> 03:06.610
That's the kind of thing...

03:06.610 --> 03:07.590
Emily?

03:07.590 --> 03:11.150
That's the kind of thing 
you need to say <i>first!</i>

03:11.150 --> 03:13.480
Huh? Wait, what do you mean?

03:19.380 --> 03:21.800
Wow, look at them all!

03:22.250 --> 03:25.080
This double drop rate is amazing!

03:33.240 --> 03:34.860
Can I help with anything?

03:35.260 --> 03:37.790
That's all right. I'll be done in no time.

03:38.250 --> 03:41.870
<i>It must be rough on her, 
having a tiny kitchen like this.</i>

03:42.700 --> 03:44.200
Hey, Emily...

03:45.130 --> 03:47.820
I think I'd like to move somewhere else.

03:49.200 --> 03:51.660
You want to move?

03:51.660 --> 03:54.220
Yeah. With what we're making now,

03:54.220 --> 03:57.090
I think it's about time 
to get a nicer place.

03:57.090 --> 03:59.530
I... I see.

03:59.910 --> 04:02.330
What kind of place would 
you like to live in?

04:02.740 --> 04:05.870
No, you can choose whatever you...

04:07.200 --> 04:09.680
I can go with you?!

04:09.680 --> 04:11.490
Well, of course.

04:11.490 --> 04:15.310
It'll be after we save a little 
more money, of course, but...

04:15.310 --> 04:16.960
It's okay to work hard,

04:17.600 --> 04:19.560
but don't work <i>too</i> hard, okay?

04:19.840 --> 04:21.320
I know.

04:21.320 --> 04:24.710
Tomorrow, I'll gather bamboo shoots again 
and get home at the usual time.

04:25.040 --> 04:25.840
Good!

04:32.120 --> 04:33.240
<i>Is that...</i>

04:33.860 --> 04:38.540
Hmm... These are a bit 
difficult to appraise.

04:38.540 --> 04:40.360
You there. Excuse me.

04:40.720 --> 04:44.140
Would you mind letting me 
have those bamboo shoots?

04:44.140 --> 04:44.980
Huh?

04:49.190 --> 04:52.370
Uh, I mean, I don't mind 
giving you one of them...

04:52.370 --> 04:55.100
Thank you. I'll just take one, then.

05:02.530 --> 05:04.460
Whoa, that was amazing!

05:11.850 --> 05:14.290
D-Does it taste that bad?

05:14.290 --> 05:17.170
Despite being raw, it's not bitter at all!

05:17.170 --> 05:21.920
It's so juicy and sweet! I've never 
had a bamboo shoot like this before!

05:21.920 --> 05:23.500
It's like... It's like...

05:24.170 --> 05:27.630
a rare monster of flavor!

05:27.630 --> 05:29.510
Who the heck is this lady?!

05:29.750 --> 05:33.790
Please let me buy all of these 
marvelous bamboo shoots.

05:33.790 --> 05:36.240
Huh? Uh, but these are...

05:36.240 --> 05:40.350
I-It's all right! 
She's welcome to have all of them!

05:40.350 --> 05:43.160
Really? Well, okay, then.

05:43.160 --> 05:44.440
Thank you!

05:44.800 --> 05:48.890
I can't put a price on 
this great flavor, so...

05:49.410 --> 05:52.530
Please accept this as a 
token of my gratitude!

05:53.070 --> 05:57.320
<i>The way this is going... 
Is she about to pay big for these?!</i>

05:59.040 --> 05:59.970
Huh?

05:59.970 --> 06:01.700
Well, thanks!

06:01.960 --> 06:04.610
Fantastic bamboo shoot boy!

06:06.330 --> 06:09.400
Twenty thousand... Twenty thousand pilos?

06:10.350 --> 06:13.370
I mean, that's a high price for 
some bamboo shoots, right?

06:13.370 --> 06:15.780
It'd be wrong of me to feel disappointed.

06:16.190 --> 06:18.320
Ryota, that lady...

06:18.320 --> 06:19.840
Was she someone important?

06:19.840 --> 06:22.030
"Important" doesn't begin to cover it!

06:22.340 --> 06:24.720
That was Eric Macy, the epicure.

06:24.720 --> 06:29.730
Any food she approves of will fetch a 
high price among the gourmet crowd!

06:29.940 --> 06:31.440
I see...

06:31.440 --> 06:34.220
Ryota, I'll skip all the formalities.

06:34.660 --> 06:37.110
Would you sign an exclusive 
contract with us?

06:37.110 --> 06:38.360
A contract?

06:38.660 --> 06:43.230
Your bamboo shoots will soon be 
a hot topic all over Secro.

06:43.230 --> 06:47.710
When that happens, I want the rights 
to sell them as a branded product.

06:47.970 --> 06:50.560
I want to sell them as 
Ryota's Bamboo Shoots!

06:51.110 --> 06:52.950
A branded product?

06:52.950 --> 06:56.860
That would be great for me, 
but are they really worth—

06:56.860 --> 06:58.030
They are!

06:58.030 --> 07:01.590
I'll pay a signing bonus in 
addition to the cost of the shoots!

07:01.590 --> 07:02.590
All right.

07:02.920 --> 07:03.680
Huh?

07:03.680 --> 07:05.680
I'll trust you with all of it.

07:06.270 --> 07:08.220
Happy to partner with you, Erza.

07:09.390 --> 07:10.430
Same!

07:11.110 --> 07:15.660
<b>Nihonium Level 1</b>

07:11.110 --> 07:15.660
Okay, gotta raise my strength 
stat some more today.

07:15.660 --> 07:18.030
I'll be at rank S soon—

07:19.080 --> 07:20.340
Who's that?

07:22.000 --> 07:23.170
Watch out!

07:23.170 --> 07:24.470
Now!

07:24.470 --> 07:25.370
Right!

07:35.600 --> 07:37.650
What the heck was that?

07:37.650 --> 07:40.110
Sorry, but try not to get in our way.

07:40.110 --> 07:43.200
Princess Margaret is on the job.

07:43.200 --> 07:44.030
Princess?

07:47.240 --> 07:52.220
You've got a princess, too? 
This world is amazing.

07:52.220 --> 07:54.480
She's using an air box.

07:54.480 --> 07:55.780
An air box?

07:55.780 --> 08:00.640
Yeah. You know how monsters sometimes
don't drop anything after you kill them?

08:00.640 --> 08:05.250
Oh, yeah... For most people, I guess 
the monsters in Nihonium don't...

08:05.730 --> 08:09.790
It's apparently a useless dungeon 
where nothing drops at all.

08:09.790 --> 08:14.890
Yep. Recent research has revealed 
that they're actually dropping air.

08:14.890 --> 08:16.320
Really?!

08:16.320 --> 08:20.720
Yeah. So we had the idea to put 
the air in a box and sell it.

08:20.720 --> 08:24.850
And it's not just any air. 
It's handmade by Princess Margaret!

08:24.850 --> 08:27.600
It's impressive that you 
had the idea to sell air.

08:27.600 --> 08:30.280
Yep! It's our top product!

08:30.640 --> 08:33.690
For real? Is this the princess effect?

08:33.960 --> 08:35.940
Is that a magic cart?

08:35.940 --> 08:39.570
Yep. It lets us carry a lot 
of air boxes at once.

08:39.570 --> 08:43.710
We can't have the princess coming in 
and out of the dungeon too much.

08:43.710 --> 08:48.960
Oh, yeah. Just being able to make fewer 
trips would make it so much easier.

08:49.450 --> 08:51.140
A magic cart...

08:51.140 --> 08:54.190
I've wanted one for ages, 
but it'd be a major purchase.

08:54.650 --> 08:57.090
I'll have to talk it over with Emily, too.

08:57.980 --> 09:03.680
So now I'm not sure whether to get 
a new house or a magic cart first.

09:03.970 --> 09:06.390
We should get a magic cart, then.

09:06.390 --> 09:08.840
If we use it to save up money,

09:08.840 --> 09:11.140
we'll be able to afford a new place soon.

09:11.140 --> 09:14.990
Good point. 
Though we'd have to put off moving,

09:14.990 --> 09:17.070
and I'd feel bad doing that to you...

09:17.070 --> 09:19.160
It's perfectly fine!

09:19.160 --> 09:24.490
I like my life with you in 
this little house very much!

09:25.350 --> 09:26.690
Emily...

09:27.300 --> 09:28.420
You're right.

09:28.680 --> 09:32.220
I guess we'll be here in the 
Emily house for a while longer.

09:32.220 --> 09:33.490
Yes!

09:33.490 --> 09:36.630
Well, then, should we go to the 
magic cart shop tomorrow?

09:36.920 --> 09:40.960
We'll be able to see the owner's 
little girl, Olga, again!

09:42.880 --> 09:44.120
Is that...

09:44.500 --> 09:46.210
It's Olga!

09:51.870 --> 09:53.270
Are you okay?

09:53.270 --> 09:55.200
Daddy... Daddy has...

09:55.200 --> 09:57.200
Did something happen to your daddy?

09:57.200 --> 10:00.130
Daddy hasn't come home.

10:00.130 --> 10:01.580
What?

10:01.580 --> 10:05.190
Did he tell you where he was going?

10:05.190 --> 10:09.630
I don't know. He said he was 
going to pick flowers.

10:09.630 --> 10:10.750
Flowers?

10:10.750 --> 10:16.060
The only place to get flower drops around 
here is a dungeon called Arsenic.

10:16.060 --> 10:18.990
So there's a good chance 
that's where he is.

10:20.110 --> 10:22.580
Let's go to Arsenic!

10:23.120 --> 10:24.210
Yes!

10:25.060 --> 10:30.060
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

10:25.060 --> 10:30.060
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

10:25.380 --> 10:27.400
I wonder how many there are...

10:27.400 --> 10:30.050
I'm talking more now than I do in the show!

10:30.060 --> 10:33.570
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

10:30.060 --> 10:33.570
<b>My Unique Skill Makes <b>Me OP
Even at Level 1</b></b>

10:31.040 --> 10:31.720
My daddy's feet are stinky!

10:31.720 --> 10:32.310
My daddy's feet are stinky!

10:32.310 --> 10:32.740
My daddy's feet are stinky!

10:32.740 --> 10:33.150
My daddy's feet are stinky!

10:33.150 --> 10:33.570
My daddy's feet are stinky!

10:33.570 --> 10:35.070
My daddy's feet are stinky!

10:35.070 --> 10:38.110
<b>Arsenic Level 1</b>

10:35.420 --> 10:37.330
So this is Arsenic.

10:40.150 --> 10:43.480
The monsters here are called 
danderocks, and they don't move.

10:43.480 --> 10:45.320
They don't attack, either.

10:45.320 --> 10:48.160
I see. Then we can—

10:49.480 --> 10:54.260
Or not. Looks like we have 
to kill them after all.

10:55.460 --> 10:57.120
The bullet bounced off?!

10:57.120 --> 10:59.090
Yoda, stand back!

11:03.140 --> 11:08.390
Of course! Between your increased power 
and the strength of that hammer...

11:08.390 --> 11:10.340
Way to go, Emily!

11:12.210 --> 11:13.480
Let's hurry.

11:13.900 --> 11:18.400
<b>Arsenic Level 1</b>

11:20.290 --> 11:23.160
There he is! That's Olga's father!

11:24.090 --> 11:25.290
You okay?!

11:25.290 --> 11:26.660
Oh, no...

11:35.090 --> 11:36.160
He's asleep!

11:36.730 --> 11:38.580
Hey, wake up!

11:39.160 --> 11:40.710
He's not waking up.

11:42.470 --> 11:44.400
E-Emily?

11:44.400 --> 11:48.360
He made Olga worry so much, 
and we find out he's...

11:48.360 --> 11:50.760
Wake up right now!

11:52.280 --> 11:54.020
What's going on?!

11:54.020 --> 11:56.340
Oh, it's you two.

11:56.340 --> 11:59.950
Darn it, I was having such a nice nap.

12:00.310 --> 12:05.700
Daddy, you left your sweet little girl 
behind to wander around where, exactly?

12:06.310 --> 12:09.000
I-I apologize!

12:09.000 --> 12:12.190
What in the world were you doing here?

12:12.190 --> 12:14.160
Olga was worried sick about you.

12:14.160 --> 12:18.800
I came to get parts for my 
incredible new magic cart prototype.

12:18.800 --> 12:22.280
Namely, heavy rocks and light rocks.

12:22.280 --> 12:26.480
I caught the heavy rock, 
but as for the light rock...

12:26.480 --> 12:31.610
Well, the danderocks blocked my path, 
and I couldn't get anywhere.

12:31.860 --> 12:35.270
A prototype? The one you mentioned before?

12:35.270 --> 12:37.570
Look there. That's it.

12:38.970 --> 12:41.600
Is that rock... flying?!

12:41.600 --> 12:45.910
Light rocks are lighter than air, 
and they're rare monsters,

12:45.910 --> 12:47.670
so I just can't get one.

12:47.670 --> 12:49.190
I see.

12:49.570 --> 12:51.570
It might be tough to do solo,

12:51.570 --> 12:53.760
but I bet two people could handle it.

12:56.740 --> 13:00.340
You're light, Emily, but your hammer's heavy!

13:00.340 --> 13:03.260
A-Are you all right, Yoda?

13:03.260 --> 13:05.230
N-No problem!

13:05.230 --> 13:08.670
I got my strength up to rank S 
in Nihonium last time.

13:09.120 --> 13:11.260
I'll try my best, too!

13:13.850 --> 13:16.990
Ah! This is what I needed!

13:17.910 --> 13:21.390
It's pretty, sure, 
but what did you need that for?

13:21.390 --> 13:23.820
Let's step outside for now.

13:25.730 --> 13:30.160
There. We'll leave it be for a 
while and watch what happens.

13:31.050 --> 13:35.590
If it turns into a stray, 
it'll float up again, won't it?

13:35.920 --> 13:38.320
There was a ceiling in the dungeon,

13:38.810 --> 13:40.410
but if it floats up from here...

13:40.410 --> 13:42.620
Yes, that's the thing.

13:42.620 --> 13:46.600
We'll just have to run in and 
grab it before it flies off.

13:46.600 --> 13:49.240
So it's all up to chance, huh?

13:49.240 --> 13:51.530
I wonder if there's anything I can do...

13:52.200 --> 13:54.450
Any minute now, I think.

13:56.470 --> 13:58.390
Time to grab my drop!

14:05.280 --> 14:07.120
Nope, we're not done yet!

14:10.270 --> 14:11.290
What the?!

14:12.960 --> 14:15.300
It might be lighter than air,

14:15.300 --> 14:17.690
but it'll fall if it has 
the weight of ice on it.

14:17.690 --> 14:19.610
Amazing, Yoda!

14:29.250 --> 14:34.180
The great artisan Orton's latest 
magic cart is complete!

14:34.180 --> 14:35.640
Take it with you.

14:35.640 --> 14:38.800
No, no! We can't accept 
such an expensive gift!

14:38.800 --> 14:40.260
Don't say that.

14:40.260 --> 14:44.140
I'm not giving you this just 
because of what you did today.

14:44.140 --> 14:46.010
Then, why?

14:46.010 --> 14:49.240
You protected our town the 
other day, remember?

14:49.240 --> 14:54.070
The hero of Secro deserves some 
kind of reward, I'd say.

14:56.740 --> 15:00.410
Take good care of my 
daddy's magic cart, okay?

15:01.380 --> 15:03.060
You two...

15:04.040 --> 15:07.760
It's a reward to you for 
all your hard work.

15:08.550 --> 15:11.170
A reward... I see.

15:11.440 --> 15:13.700
I'll use it with all my gratitude!

15:18.210 --> 15:19.260
All right.

15:23.340 --> 15:25.980
Oops, looks like it's over capacity.

15:25.980 --> 15:30.520
We've gathered over twice as many bamboo 
shoots as usual thanks to the magic cart.

15:30.520 --> 15:33.380
Man, this thing is incredibly handy!

15:33.380 --> 15:34.680
Isn't it?

15:34.680 --> 15:36.770
We must be grateful to Orton and Olga.

15:36.770 --> 15:37.990
For sure.

15:37.990 --> 15:42.570
I'm gonna run over to Erza's 
place and sell her these.

15:42.570 --> 15:46.740
Then I'll head home and 
start making dinner.

15:49.520 --> 15:51.150
Gimme a break!

15:51.640 --> 15:56.560
Sir, as I've told you several times, 
there's no mistake in this purchase—

15:57.090 --> 15:58.430
Shut your mouth!

15:58.430 --> 16:02.040
I brought enough to sell for 
more than 10,000 pilos!

16:01.140 --> 16:03.200
Can't someone stop him?

16:02.040 --> 16:04.930
I bet you're lying about the price anyway!

16:03.200 --> 16:06.480
Not me. What if he tries to 
pick a fight with me next?

16:04.930 --> 16:06.490
C'mon, cough up the cash already!

16:06.760 --> 16:10.020
I'm willing to accept 
20,000 for my trouble.

16:10.020 --> 16:16.500
I can't pay more than the list price of 
8,400 pilos for what you've brought in.

16:16.500 --> 16:17.620
What?!

16:17.870 --> 16:20.680
You tryin' to go against 
a customer's word?!

16:24.350 --> 16:25.930
What the hell?!

16:26.550 --> 16:28.410
You need to stop.

16:28.410 --> 16:29.430
Ryota!

16:29.430 --> 16:30.580
The hell are you?!

16:31.030 --> 16:34.590
Erza wouldn't lie about the list price.

16:34.590 --> 16:36.340
I'll prove it to you.

16:39.930 --> 16:44.310
Check that out! 
It's Orton's latest magic cart!

16:44.720 --> 16:46.880
How does he have so many bamboo shoots?

16:47.220 --> 16:49.880
What the hell do you think you're doing?

16:56.830 --> 17:00.150
Erza, how much is one of 
these green onions worth?

17:00.150 --> 17:02.620
Huh? It's 120 pilos.

17:02.620 --> 17:03.780
Got it.

17:04.290 --> 17:09.350
This magic cart was made with 
rare monsters from Arsenic, right?

17:09.930 --> 17:12.590
So it automatically detects 
the weight of its contents

17:12.590 --> 17:15.150
and calculates the total 
amount they'll sell for.

17:17.380 --> 17:19.310
8,400 pilos.

17:19.310 --> 17:22.840
Sounds like the exact amount she quoted.

17:22.840 --> 17:26.350
You're in with this shop to 
run some scam, aren't you?!

17:26.350 --> 17:30.420
I just happened to walk in here while you 
were here. You think I could pull that off?

17:30.420 --> 17:33.560
Shut up, you little bamboo shoot bastard!

17:34.930 --> 17:38.490
I'll knock your ass off!

17:38.490 --> 17:40.410
Ryota, watch out!

17:41.620 --> 17:42.670
What?!

17:42.670 --> 17:45.570
Sorry, but I'm gonna need 
you to take a little nap.

17:49.170 --> 17:50.700
Whoa!

17:50.700 --> 17:51.510
He just saved her!

17:55.710 --> 17:58.100
You had to bail me out again.

17:58.100 --> 18:00.300
You don't need to worry about that.

18:00.300 --> 18:01.820
But I will.

18:01.820 --> 18:04.510
I'm an item trader.

18:05.220 --> 18:11.000
All the items I sell here were gathered 
at risk of life and limb by adventurers.

18:11.450 --> 18:15.040
I'm obligated to handle 
them with utmost care.

18:15.580 --> 18:19.490
I want people to feel comfortable 
bringing their goods here to sell to me.

18:20.250 --> 18:23.570
But if I have to be helped 
out all the time...

18:24.070 --> 18:27.330
It's a bit more than even I can bear.

18:27.920 --> 18:29.970
What's wrong with that?

18:29.970 --> 18:30.710
Huh?

18:31.130 --> 18:33.760
What's wrong with having help?

18:33.760 --> 18:35.360
Everyone needs help.

18:35.760 --> 18:38.460
You've helped me out a bunch, too.

18:38.830 --> 18:41.540
No, really...

18:42.030 --> 18:44.890
I haven't done anything special at all.

18:44.890 --> 18:48.190
You always buy my items 
off of me with a smile.

18:48.190 --> 18:50.100
You share your cheer with me.

18:50.840 --> 18:52.020
Ryota...

18:52.810 --> 18:57.780
And if anything like this happens 
again, I want to protect you.

18:57.780 --> 19:00.780
You scratch my back, 
I scratch yours, right?

19:02.030 --> 19:03.090
Right...

19:03.420 --> 19:09.470
Of course, I feel like the help 
you give me means a lot more...

19:19.410 --> 19:22.540
Huh?! Um, Erza?!

19:22.540 --> 19:26.160
That wasn't from me as an item trader.

19:26.160 --> 19:28.710
That was a personal kiss from me.

19:29.190 --> 19:31.810
Make sure you remember it 
after you leave here, okay?

19:32.660 --> 19:35.150
Well, I need to get back to work.

19:45.370 --> 19:48.450
<b>Telulu Level 4</b>

19:54.410 --> 19:59.340
Before, the most we could make 
in one haul was 20,000 pilos.

19:59.340 --> 20:00.460
But now...

20:05.800 --> 20:07.400
T-Two hundred thousand?!

20:07.400 --> 20:10.550
We could buy more than 6,000 
bean sprouts with that!

20:10.550 --> 20:12.570
With this much saved up...

20:12.570 --> 20:15.120
We have enough for a new house!

20:24.330 --> 20:26.980
I guess it's time to say 
goodbye to this house.

20:27.500 --> 20:29.920
It's a bit sad, isn't it?

20:30.320 --> 20:31.640
Yeah.

20:32.560 --> 20:35.290
I have lots of memories here.

20:35.570 --> 20:42.510
Yes, and I learned just how nice it 
is to have a place to come home to.

20:42.510 --> 20:44.590
Yeah. Me, too.

20:46.640 --> 20:48.120
<i>Two hundred thousand pilos...</i>

20:48.120 --> 20:50.430
<i>After killing slimes for three days,</i>

20:50.430 --> 20:54.050
<i>we finally scraped together 
200,000 pilos for rent.</i>

20:54.440 --> 20:58.080
<i>It's no small amount, but...</i>

20:58.590 --> 20:59.820
Yoda?

21:01.680 --> 21:02.620
Emily...

21:03.710 --> 21:06.400
Let's keep our lease on this place.

21:06.400 --> 21:08.860
That way we can come back home anytime,

21:08.860 --> 21:11.420
even after we move to our new house.

21:11.890 --> 21:15.780
Can we? Wouldn't that be expensive, though?

21:15.780 --> 21:19.310
I think the whole reason we've been 
dungeon-diving to make money

21:19.310 --> 21:21.710
was for a time just like this.

21:22.150 --> 21:25.380
I want to use it to protect the 
place that's precious to us.

21:25.890 --> 21:27.260
Yoda...

21:39.890 --> 21:41.950
Morning, Emily.

21:42.240 --> 21:44.930
Good morning, Yoda!

21:44.930 --> 21:46.610
Breakfast is ready.

21:47.610 --> 21:50.280
You still make the best 
breakfasts ever, Emily!

21:50.500 --> 21:53.610
I think her carrot dishes 
are the best, too.

21:53.960 --> 21:56.290
When did you come in?!

21:56.290 --> 21:59.120
Where there are carrots, 
there are also rabbits.

22:00.280 --> 22:02.950
I made lots, so it's no problem at all.

22:03.590 --> 22:06.260
Sheesh... I guess that's that.

22:06.630 --> 22:08.440
Let's eat!
